  "job_B1.4.18_20251001_193232": {
    "text": "\u00d0\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes eard w\u00e6s on Iudea lande, Galileiscre scire, \u00fea \u00fea he her on life w\u00e6s, on \u00fe\u00e6re byrig\n\u00d0a ferde he geond eall \u00fe\u00e6re fores\u00e6dan scire, to eallum samnungum, symle l\u00e6rende \u00fe\u00e6t folc, &\nHis hlisa \u00fea asprang to Sirian lande, ofer eall \u00fe\u00e6t rice, \u00fe\u00e6t is swi\u00fee rum land; & him man gebrohte \u00fea\nNu seg\u00f0 us se godspellere \u00fee \u00feiss godspell gesette \u00fee nu gebira\u00f0 to \u00feissere m\u00e6ssan, MARCVS gehaten\n\u00d0a gebrohte man him to, tomiddes \u00feam folce, \u00e6nne dumne mann, & se w\u00e6s eac swilce deaf, & b\u00e6don\nHe dyde \u00fea his fingras innto his earan, & mid his halwendan spatle hys tungan hrepode, & beseah to\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea, sona wurdon his earan geopenode, & his tungan bend wear\u00f0 unbunden eac, & he rihtlice\n\u00d0a bebead se H\u00e6lend \u00feam \u00fee hine brohton \u00fe\u00e6t hi hit ne s\u00e6don nanum menn nateshwon; ac hi \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fee\n\u00d0iss godspell is nu ges\u00e6d \u00feuss sceortlice on Englisc; nu wylle we geedl\u00e6can eft \u00fea ylcan word \u00fe\u00e6s\nTirus & Sidon syndon twa burga, be \u00feam spr\u00e6c se H\u00e6lend on sumere stowe hwilon, \u00fea \u00fea he cidde\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00fe\u00e6re byrig \u00fee hatte Corozaim, & to anre o\u00f0re byrig, Bethsaida gehaten, Wa \u00fee, Corozaim;\nNu secge ic to so\u00fean \u00fe\u00e6t sumera \u00feinga by\u00fe l\u00e6sse wite on Domesd\u00e6g Tyro & Sidone \u00feonne eow sylfum\nSe H\u00e6lend geneal\u00e6hte to \u00feam s\u00e6lende to \u00feam worigendum y\u00feum, \u00f0e h\u00e6fdon getacnunge \u00fe\u00e6re\nAn eard w\u00e6s gehaten \u00fea on eastd\u00e6le, begeondan \u00fe\u00e6re ea iordanen decapolis on bocum, \u00fe\u00e6t is Tyn\n\u00d0es deafa mann getacnode & \u00fees dumba witodlice eall Adames cynn, \u00fee adeafode swi\u00fee \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6re\nMancynn adumbode eac fram his Drihtenes herungum sy\u00fe\u00fean he \u00e6ne gespr\u00e6c his agen bep\u00e6cend, &\nNe mihte na se deafa ne se dumba abiddan \u00feone halgan H\u00e6lend his agene h\u00e6le; ac his magas b\u00e6don, \u00fee\nSwa we sceolon eac don, gif sum ure freonda ne m\u00e6g \u00feurh hine sylfne secan \u00e6t his Drihtene his sawle\n\u00d0iss halige godspell seg\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t se H\u00e6lend sona gel\u00e6dde \u00feone mann ut of \u00fe\u00e6re meniu, for \u00fean \u00fee he\nHe dyde \u00fea his fingras innto his earan.\n\u00d0\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes fingras, \u00fee halwende syndon, getacnia\u00f0 so\u00f0lice \u00fea seofonfealdan gyfa \u00fe\u00e6s Halgan\nMid his halwendan spatle he hrepode his tungan, \u00fe\u00e6t he sprecan mihte, & mannum eac cy\u00fean godes\nHe beseah to heofonum, & s\u00e6de mid geomerunge to \u00feam dumban menn \u00feis an dyrne word: Effeta:\nTo heofonum he beseah mid swi\u00felicere geomerunge, for \u00fean \u00fee he gesceop him sylf us \u00e6t fruman to\nHe geswutelode eac mid his sylfes geomerunge \u00fe\u00e6t we sceolon gewilnian \u00fe\u00e6re heofonlican wununge,\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea effeta, \u00fe\u00e6t ys to geopenigenne, for \u00fe\u00e6re deafnysse \u00fee him derode o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t; ac his\nBe \u00fe\u00e6re ylcan d\u00e6de do\u00f0 git Godes \u00feenas \u00feonne hi cild fullia\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t hi setta\u00f0 heora fingras innan \u00fe\u00e6s\n\u00d0\u00e6t spatl getacna\u00f0, swa swa \u00fees traht seg\u00f0, \u00feone upplican wisdom \u00fee hit gewilnian sceal, & \u00fe\u00e6re\nBe \u00feam ilcan gecw\u00e6\u00f0 se eadiga Iob: Swa lange swa seo ore\u00f0ung is on us wunigende, & Godes Gast\nHw\u00e6t, \u00fea sona wurdon his earan geopenode, & his tungan bend wear\u00f0 unbunden eac, & he rihtlice\nWe spreca\u00f0 rihtlice on rihtum geleafan, \u00fe\u00e6t we rihtlice gelyfon on \u00feone lyfigendan God, & we hine\nNu sceole we hogian \u00fe\u00e6t we hine ne gremion \u00e6fter urum fulluhte ealles to swi\u00fee, \u00feurh unrihtwise\n\u00d0a bebead se H\u00e6lend \u00feam \u00fee hine brohton \u00fe\u00e6t hi hit ne s\u00e6don nanum menn nateshwon; ac hi \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fee\nSe H\u00e6lend, \u00fee mihte swylce wundra gefremman, mihte eac don \u00fe\u00e6t hi digle w\u00e6ron; ac he bebead \u00feam\nSe idela gylp huru is an heafodleahter, gode swi\u00f0e s\u00e6don s\u00e6te, & we eac sceolon \u00feone yfelan un\u00feeaw\nWe wylla\u00f0 eow gereccan sume Cristes wundra, to getrymminge eowres geleafan.\nVre Drihten stah on scyp, & him fyligdon his leorningcnihtas.\nEfne \u00fea f\u00e6rlice aras mycel styrung & hreohness on \u00fe\u00e6re s\u00e6, swa \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t scyp wear\u00f0 mid y\u00feum\nSe wind witodlice heom stod ongean mid orm\u00e6tum bl\u00e6de.\nAnd se H\u00e6lend wear\u00f0 on sl\u00e6pe on \u00feam steorsetle.\n\u00d0a geneal\u00e6hton his leorningcnihtas & hine awrehton, \u00feuss cwe\u00f0ende: Drihten, gehelp ure; we losia\u00f0.\nHe andwyrde, Eala ge lytles geleafan, to hwi synd ge afyrhte?\nHe aras \u00fea, & \u00feywde \u00feone wind & \u00fea s\u00e6, & het hi stille beon.\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea sona wear\u00f0 geworden mycel smyltnyss on \u00fe\u00e6re sae, swa \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea re\u00f0ran, micclum\nSe H\u00e6lend geswutelode mid \u00feam sl\u00e6pe \u00fea so\u00fean menniscnysse, & mid \u00feam wundre his godcundan\nHe slep swa swa so\u00f0 mann, & he \u00fea y\u00feiendan s\u00e6 mid anre h\u00e6se gestilde swa swa \u00e6lmihtig Scyppend,\nHi \u00fea oferreowon \u00feone brym & gelendon on \u00feam lande \u00fee is gehaten Gerasenorum.\nEfne \u00fea \u00fea hi upp eodon, arn \u00fe\u00e6r an wod mann togeanes \u00feam H\u00e6lende, se h\u00e6fde wununge on\nHe wunode on dunum d\u00e6ges & nihtes, & on byrgenum, hrymende, & beatende hine sylfne mid\nHe arn \u00fea to \u00feam H\u00e6lende, \u00fea \u00fea he hine geseah, & feoll to his fotum, mid mycelre stemne clypiende,\nSe H\u00e6lend him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, \u00f0u uncl\u00e6na gast, gewit of \u00feam menn.\nAnd he hine \u00fea befran hw\u00e6t his nama w\u00e6re.\n\u00d0a andwyrde se uncl\u00e6na gast \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6s wodan mu\u00f0, & cw\u00e6\u00f0, Min nama is eorod, for \u00fean \u00fee we her\nAnd b\u00e6d hine \u00fea micclum \u00fe\u00e6t he hine of \u00feam earde ne adr\u00e6fde.\n\u00d0a stod \u00fe\u00e6r onemm \u00f0a dune micel heord swyna, & \u00fea deofla b\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t hi moston into \u00f0am swynum.\n\u00dea ge\u00f0afode se H\u00e6lend \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0am deoflum.\nAnd hi gewiton of \u00f0am men into \u00f0am swynum.\n\u00dea swyn \u00f0a ealle endemes scuton into \u00fe\u00e6re s\u00e6, sume twa \u00feusend, & \u00fe\u00e6r adruncon \u00feurh \u00feone\n\u00d0a swanas flugon afyrhte to \u00fe\u00e6re byrig, & cyddon be \u00feam swynum, & be \u00feam witseocan menn.\n\u00d0a comon \u00fea ceastergewaran sona to \u00feam H\u00e6lende, & gesawon \u00feone wodan mann wel gescrydne, &\n\u00d0a gewende Crist to scype, & se gewitseoca hine b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t he moste mid him.\nDrihten him andwyrde, Far \u00fee ham to \u00feinum hiwum, & cy\u00fe heom hu mycele mihte Drihten on \u00fee\nHe \u00fea ferde, swi\u00fee bodigende Drihtenes wundra, and menn \u00fe\u00e6s wundredon.\nAn eorod is on bocum geteald to syx \u00feusendum, & swa fela awrygedra gasta w\u00e6ron \u00feam anum menn\n\u00d0a deoflu oncneowon urne H\u00e6lend Crist, & \u00fe\u00e6t Iudeisce folc hine dwollice wi\u00f0soc, & syndon for\u00fei\nNe dorston \u00fea deoflu, \u00fea \u00fea hi adr\u00e6fde w\u00e6ron, into \u00feam swynum, gyf he heom ne sealde leafe, ne into\n\u00d0a swyn hi gecuron for heora sweartum hiwe, & for \u00fe\u00e6re fulnesse fenlices adelan.\nSe mann \u00fee h\u00e6f\u00f0 swynes \u00feeawas, & wyle hine a\u00fewean mid wope fram synnum, & eft hine befylan\nSe \u00fee oft gegrema\u00f0 God \u00feurh leahtras, & \u00e6fre geedl\u00e6c\u00f0 his yfelan d\u00e6da, he by\u00fe swyne gelic, &\nUton we herian urne Drihten symle on his micclum wundrum, & us miltsunge biddan, & yfel forl\u00e6tan,\nWe wylla\u00f0 eow gyt secgan sum wundor be Criste, & \u00feas geendunge eallswa geglengan, anfealdum\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6r w\u00e6s \u00fea an wod mann on \u00fe\u00e6re gesamnunge mid \u00feam fulan gaste deoflice afylled, & se\n\u00deu come to fordonne & to amyrrenne us.\nEala ic wat geare \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu eart Godes Halga.\nSe H\u00e6lend \u00fea sona \u00fereade \u00feone deofol, \u00feuss him secgende: Swiga \u00feu hra\u00f0e, & gewit aweg of \u00feisum\n\u00d0a wear\u00f0 mycel oga on eallum \u00feam mannum, & hi swi\u00fee spr\u00e6con, secgende heom betwynan, Hw\u00e6t\n\u00d0a wear\u00f0 gewidm\u00e6rsod wide his hlisa on \u00e6lcere stowe ealles \u00fe\u00e6s eardes.\nSwylce wundra worhte se welwillenda H\u00e6lend her on \u00feisum life, to geleafan trymminge, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea\nAMEN.",
